meta {
  name: 03 Patient Login
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/patient-portal/auth/login
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "identifier": "{{patientLoginIdentifier}}",
    "password": "Password@123"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  const data = body && body.data;
  if (data && data.bootstrapToken) {
    bru.setEnvVar("patientBootstrapToken", data.bootstrapToken);
  }
}

docs {
  **Patient portal — step 1 of 2 ("login then pick business").** Authenticates the
  platform identity (no tenant yet). Separate `'jwt-patient'` auth system; a
  patient token is rejected on every business/SiteAdmin route by construction.

  Fields:
  - `identifier` (required) — registered mobile or email (precedence mobile →
    email).
  - `password` (required) — the staff-issued temp password on first login
    (`Password@123`), or the patient's chosen password afterwards.

  Returns `data`: `{ bootstrapToken, mustChangePassword, businesses[] }`, where
  `businesses` is `{ tenantId, tenantName, tenantSlug, shortName, logoUrl }[]`.
  Captures `patientBootstrapToken`. Exchange it at **Select Business**.

  Enforces the shared lockout (10 fails → 15 min). Errors: `401
  PATIENT_INVALID_CREDENTIALS`; `423 PATIENT_ACCOUNT_LOCKED`; `403
  PATIENT_ACCOUNT_INACTIVE`; `403 PATIENT_NO_LOGIN_ACCESS` (identity not enrolled
  as a patient anywhere — staff must run **Issue Patient Credentials** first).
}
